PRETABLE11 ADDENDUM 3 -- 2026-09-06 ~12:20, written BEFORE table 11's second launch (attempt 1 aborted at BASE; its output is preserved
in killtable11_attempt1_v13/, nothing else ran).

WHAT HAPPENED.  The driver's BASE gate read 45/46 on frozen v13 (md5 4192b7da) and aborted, as designed: row errc RESULT=BADREGS
pc=0x50 sxip=0x10006 snip=0x1000a sfip=0x1000e psr=0x9000000b epsr=0x80000002 bad=psr.  The row was DELIVERED to ERROR at 0x50 with
frozen shadows and the refatal line -- everything the row exists to pin -- and failed only on its PSR expectation, which was the
default PSR_EXC 0x8000000b.  Exception entry ORs MODE|SFRZ|IND|SFD1 into PSR and leaves the carry bit alone (mc88100 manual, grep
'the shadow freeze, SFD1, and IND bits of the PSR are set'; the fork's common path does exactly that), so a handler that set C keeps
C: the correct expectation is 0x9000000b.  The sibling ovfc row already documents the same point from the other side ('PSR ==
0x8000000b pinned C NOT SET, never C unchanged').

DISPOSITION.  A mutant-that-will-not-die case 3 in its BASE form -- THE ROW IS MIS-CUT, not the fix and not a mutant.  Repaired in
the instrument only: PSR_WANT["errc"] = 0x9000000b (probe v14, md5 in the driver log; the frozen v13 is kept for the record).  No
product code touched; no mutant re-aimed.  The BASE gate is what this driver's first step is for, and it fired.

UNCHANGED.  Seven mutants, WANT=46/46, each also scored on frozen v10; the errc CHANNEL under M_RRNOC is unchanged (entry pc 0x20 vs
0x50 plus the refatal line) -- the PSR field is not the channel, so the repair cannot have made the row vacuous: under M_RRNOC the
row still reds on RESULT (breakpoint at 0x50 never reached).
